    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "VF/pulseless VT: if 2 shocks fail, epinephrine 1 mg IV, repeated every 3 to 5 minutes; defibrillate 1 to 2 minutes after each dose."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "If VF persists, amiodarone 300 mg IV; if VF/VT recurs, 150 mg, then an infusion."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Lidocaine is an alternative to amiodarone for VF/VT that doesn't respond to defibrillation and epinephrine."
     }
    ]
   }
  ]
 },
